    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="0679" n="563" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12497.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to Mexico to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 15, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. This afternoon General Huerta will resign and Carbajal, the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs mentioned in my 82, July 10, will take possession as Provisional
                    President, with best disposition to facilitate arrangements for the
                    pacification. Department’s views will be highly appreciated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
